Claim: Cash flows are exposed to competition, commodity and trade-policy volatility: the company faces significant global competition with the risk of market share decline, purchases all of its natural rubber requirements in the world market, and has been negatively impacted by changes in tariffs and trade restrictions as well as raw material, energy and transportation cost increases.

